  "notes": "{二度|にど} means \"twice\" or \"two times.\" It can also express \"never again\" in a specific grammatical pattern.\n\nKEY PATTERN:\n{二度|にど}と + negative verb = never again. This expresses strong resolve or emotional emphasis:\n- {二度|にど}と{行|い}かない: I'll never go again\n- {二度|にど}と{会|あ}いたくない: I never want to see them again\n- {二度|にど}と{繰|く}り{返|かえ}さない: I'll never repeat this\n\nPROVERB:\n{二度|にど}あることは{三度|さんど}ある: What happens twice will happen a third time (similar to \"things come in threes\").\n\nRELATED COUNTING WORDS:\n- {一度|いちど}: once\n- {三度|さんど}: three times\n- {何度|なんど}: how many times\n- {何度|なんど}も: many times, repeatedly",
